.TH PANORA-DOCTOR 1 "2026-09-19" "panora" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
panora-doctor \- diagnose a Panora installation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B panora-doctor
.RB [ \-\-json " | " \-\-report\fR[=\fIFILE\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B panora-doctor
checks the operating system, the session type, the installed binaries,
.BR panod.service ,
the IPC socket, the active backend, the GNOME Shell extension, the D-Bus
names, the Secret Service, the Super+V shortcut, the data directory and the
configuration. Every check prints one line
.RB ( OK ", " WARN ", " ERROR " or " INFO )
with a suggested command when something is wrong. It never modifies anything.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the checks as one JSON document instead of text.
.TP
.BR \-\-report [=\fIFILE\fR]
Write a diagnostic file for a bug report (default name
.IB panora-report- DATE .txt
in the current directory): the checks in English, versions, session
variables, the daemon status, the unit state, the last 200 lines of the panod
journal, the extension state and the configuration. The home directory, the
user name and the host name are replaced, the values of
.B ignore_patterns
are left out, and no clipboard content is read. The file is created with mode
0600; review it before attaching it to an issue.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
unless the daemon itself is unusable (not running, no socket, or
.B panora-cli status
failing); warnings never change the exit status.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PANORA_LANG
Force the message language
.RB ( en " or " tr );
otherwise the locale decides.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR panod (1),
.BR panora-cli (1)
.SH BUGS
https://github.com/ygkali/panora/issues
